# inc-7wmu S5: a re-apply must not cost the wearer hit points. Read by
# tools/check_reapply_single_grant.sh, seed 1. Expected to PASS on the unfixed
# engine; it exists to turn red if a fix strips the wearer's rows without
# guarding HP.
#
# THE HAZARD. A Girdle of Tenacity (lib/m_items.irh:275) grants ADJUST/A_CON
# at 1 per plus. CalcValues keeps DAMAGE, not current HP: cHP -= mHP, rebuild mHP,
# cHP += mHP (src/Values.cpp:1800,1863), and cHP <= 0 there is a death or a DC
# 20 Fortitude save to 1 HP (:1865). Worn at +2 on base CON 12 the girdle lifts
# CON to 14 and max HP 77 -> 85 (6 levels x 1 x 1.25 Toughness). At 7 HP, a
# re-apply that drops those rows for even one CalcValues takes HP to -1.
# Enchanting to +3 makes CON 15, whose modifier is still +2, so a correct
# re-apply leaves HP at exactly 7. The unfixed engine adds a +3 row beside
# the +2 one; the max rule for typed bonuses hides it, so HP stays 7 there too.
#
# LOW HP. Divine Sacrifice's HP cost moved from cast time to attack time
# (inc-l8ws): casting alone no longer lowers HP, so the setup instead pays
# by attacking. Wizard "Learn Any Spell" (src/Debug.cpp, case 17) teaches
# Divine Sacrifice (lib/pspells.irh:1149) as an innate spell; the Freeze
# Monsters wizard switch holds a summoned froghemoth still so every bump is
# an attack that can pay. Each round the caster attacks, Divine Sacrifice
# pays the chosen 10 HP once (lib/pspells.irh's META(EV_STRIKE): at most
# once per round, never a payment that would reach 0 HP or below), so four
# recast-and-attack cycles settle HP at 85 mod 10 = 5 with no randomness,
# whatever the exact per-cycle payment count. Below the pinned low-HP
# threshold every drop raises a "Low Hitpoint Warning!" box that waits for a
# key (src/Player.cpp:275-285).
#
# THE RE-APPLY is Storycraft -> SetInherentPlus -> Item::ReApply, the same
# path as reapply-enchant.keys, whose header cites it line by line. It spends
# no game time for a bard, so natural healing cannot move HP between dumps.
#
# inc-stzd: this used to @include reapply-bard.keys; see reapply-enchant.keys's
# header for why it now starts from the same INCURSION_LOAD fixture instead
# (tools/fixtures/chars/orc-bard-reapply-seed1.sav) -- that script's own CON
# base of 12, which this section's HP arithmetic depends on, is unchanged.

d
@dump:sheet-without-girdle
ESC

w
@choose "Item Acquisition"
RIGHT*25                # girdles: -AI_GIRDLE in ItemGlyphs, src/Tables.cpp:346
@until "Girdle of Tenacity" DOWN
DOWN ENTER              # three rows show and the middle one is taken
2 ENTER                 # "Enter Item Level:" sets the plus
g SPACE                 # Belt
@dump:girdle-worn
ESC

d
@dump:sheet-with-girdle
ESC

w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Divine Sacrifice" ENTER
@dump:learned

w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*10 SPACE            # Freeze Monsters: NO -> YES
ESC

u
@choose "Innate Divine Sacrifice" 5
@dump:cast-1

